> Actual source performance

These measurements come from the complete source run above; each series retains source execution order. A bounded run or one evaluation point does not establish convergence. Model loss and task return use separate figures.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/mpc_diagnostic0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto data=dm::nn::load_npz("build/mpc_source.npz");auto it=std::find_if(data.begin(),data.end(),[](const auto&v){return v.first=="episode_return";});auto all=it->second.to_vector<double>();auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();for(int method=0;method<2;++method){std::vector<double>x,y;for(size_t j=2+method;j<all.size();j+=2){x.push_back((j-2)/2+1);y.push_back(all[j]);}plot.lines(x,y,method?"CEM":"random shooting",{37+method*150,99,235-method*150});}plot.title("MPC original planner comparison").x_label("Collect/refit round").y_label("Task return").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/mpc_diagnostic0.svg");}
